---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SidebarLayout from "../components/SidebarLayout.astro";
import Sidebar from "../components/Sidebar.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import { PRIVACY_UPDATED_AT } from "../lib/privacy";
import { listPostSummaries, listCategoriesWithPostCounts } from "../lib/content";

// Text-only page: share the blog sidebar so the panel isn't mostly empty.
const [categories, posts] = await Promise.all([
  listCategoriesWithPostCounts(Astro.locals),
  listPostSummaries(Astro.locals, 5),
]);
const recentPosts = posts.map((p) => ({
  slug: p.slug,
  title: p.title,
  dateLabel: new Date(p.publishedAt ?? p.createdAt).toLocaleDateString("en-US", { year: "numeric", month: "long", day: "numeric" }),
}));
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Orboro.net" description="Privacy policy for Orboro.net">
  <PageHeader slot="hero" title="Privacy Policy">
    <span>Last updated: <time datetime={PRIVACY_UPDATED_AT}>{new Date(`${PRIVACY_UPDATED_AT}T00:00:00Z`).toLocaleDateString("en-US", { year: "numeric", month: "long", day: "numeric", timeZone: "UTC" })}</time></span>
  </PageHeader>
  <SidebarLayout>
  <section class="prose">

    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      Orboro.net is a personal site operated by JD. You can read its public pages without
      an account. An optional member account lets you comment and vote. The site uses
      Cloudflare for hosting, security checks and account email, and Google Analytics for
      usage measurement. This policy describes the information involved in those services,
      member accounts and comments, administrator login, and requests to external image providers.
    </p>

    <h2>Information collected</h2>
    <h3>Hosting and diagnostics</h3>
    <p>
      Cloudflare processes requests to deliver pages and images and operate its network.
      Request information can include your IP address, the requested URL, browser details,
      and referring information. Worker request/error logging and sampled tracing are enabled
      to diagnose failures and monitor operation. On the site's current Cloudflare plan, Worker
      logs are kept for 7 days, and no log export to other services is configured. Cloudflare's
      own network records follow its service terms, and plan or setting changes can change these
      periods, so this site does not promise a fixed deletion period for those records.
    </p>

    <h3>Analytics</h3>
    <p>
      Google Analytics measures visits and pages viewed and can collect browser/device details,
      referring information and approximate location. Google's tag uses cookies and browser
      identifiers to distinguish visits. These identifiers mean the collection should not be
      treated as completely anonymous, even when reports show aggregate statistics.
    </p>
    <p>
      Analytics loads on public pages only after
      you accept analytics cookies in the consent banner. Declining keeps the analytics tag
      from loading. Your choice is saved in this browser's local storage until you change
      it or clear that storage. Without JavaScript, the analytics tag does not load. Page-view
      events send the page title, the page address without any query parameters or fragment,
      and the previous page address in the same reduced form. Google's tag can still collect
      other browser details described above. The administrator login screen, the
      administration interface and sign-in endpoints do not load the analytics tag.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site's tag configuration keeps advertising storage, advertising user data, and
      advertising personalization consent denied, even when you accept analytics.
      The site code does not include a separate advertising pixel.
    </p>
    <p>
      As of the date of this policy, the Google Analytics property keeps event-level data for
      2 months and user-level data for 14 months, extended while a returning browser stays
      active. Google signals is off, and the property is linked to no advertising product;
      its only product link is Google Search Console. Sharing analytics data with Google to
      improve Google's products is off. Google may still use aggregated, de-identified data
      for modeling and benchmarks, Google support staff may access the account when asked to
      help, and Google may use account usage information to make recommendations. Reports
      built from aggregated data can be kept longer than these periods.
    </p>
    <p>
      After you accept, your browser loads Google's current analytics script directly from
      Google. Google updates that script, so the site cannot pin or verify its exact contents
      the way it does its own files. The site's security policy only accepts that script from
      Google's tag domain, so a script from another host cannot take its place.
    </p>

    <p>
      You can opt out of Google Analytics tracking using
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Google's browser opt-out add-on
      </a>, or with any browser extension that blocks third-party analytics scripts.
    </p>

    <h3>Member accounts</h3>
    <p>
      Creating an account stores, in Cloudflare D1, your username, email address, a password hash,
      the account's creation date and whether the email is confirmed, plus an optional display name
      and bio if you add them. Your email address is never shown publicly and is used only to confirm
      the address, to confirm a change of address, to send password-reset links, and to tell you if
      someone tries to register with it. Those emails are sent through Cloudflare's Email Service.
      Links in them carry a single-use token that expires (48 hours to confirm a sign-up address,
      24 hours for an address change, 1 hour for a password reset); the database keeps only a one-way
      digest of each token.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you choose a password, its strength is checked against the
      <a href="https://haveibeenpwned.com/API/v3#PwnedPasswords" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pwned Passwords</a>
      service, which receives only the first five characters of the password's SHA-1 hash and never
      the password itself. The registration and password-reset forms use
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Turnstile</a>
      to tell people from automated sign-ups; it runs a check in your browser and may process browser
      and device signals to do so. To limit abuse, the site counts sign-in, registration, email and
      commenting attempts per IP address, account or member in windows of up to an hour; the
      counters store only one-way digests of those values and are deleted after their window ends.
    </p>
    <p>
      Signing in sets an <code>__Host-orboro_member</code> cookie that keeps you signed in for up to
      14 days. It is HttpOnly, Secure, and uses SameSite=Lax. Signing out revokes that session, and
      <strong>Sign out everywhere</strong> on your account page revokes all of them.
    </p>

    <h3>Comments, votes and profiles</h3>
    <p>
      Comments are public. Each one shows your display name or username and when it was posted or
      edited, and your profile page at <code>/u/your-username</code> shows your display name, bio,
      join date, comment count, karma (the net votes other members gave your comments) and recent
      comments. Votes are stored with your account so you can change them, but who voted on what is
      not shown to other members. Reports you file are visible only to the administrator.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can edit or delete your comments, and change your profile, email or password, on your
      account page. Deleting a comment that has replies leaves an empty [deleted] placeholder so the
      thread still reads; a comment without replies is removed. Deleting your account removes your
      email address, password hash, profile, votes, reports and sessions, and erases the text of your
      comments, which remain in their threads as [deleted] without your name. The administrator can
      remove comments that break the site's rules, and suspend or delete accounts.
    </p>

    <h3>Administrator account and session</h3>
    <p>
      The administrator account belongs to JD and is separate from member accounts; members can't
      sign in to the administration area. Cloudflare D1 stores the administrator's email, a password
      hash, and session records that hold a one-way digest of each session token. Successful login sets an
      <code>__Host-orboro_session</code> cookie to keep the administrator signed in for up to
      14 days. It is HttpOnly, Secure, and uses SameSite=Lax. Logging out revokes that session
      and removes the cookie. Reading public pages does not require either login cookie.
    </p>

    <h3>Third-party links</h3>
    <p>
      This site contains links to external platforms (Reddit, Discord, official game sites, and
      similar resources). Once you leave this site, this privacy policy no longer applies. Please review
      the privacy practices of those platforms directly.
    </p>

    <h3>Bookmark lists (Tagstash)</h3>
    <p>
      Various "Useful Links" pages (for individual games, FOSS software, and similar topics) display bookmarks pulled from
      <a href="https://tagsta.sh/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tagstash</a>, a bookmarking
      service. Bookmark data is fetched by this site's server and cached for ten minutes.
      That API request does not forward your browser cookies, IP address or request headers.
      Your browser loads bookmark favicons directly from the image URLs supplied by Tagstash;
      the Tagstash credit icon uses Google's favicon service. Those image hosts receive your
      IP address and browser request details. The favicon requests omit the referring page URL.
    </p>

    <h3>Images and publication updates</h3>
    <p>
      Site uploads are stored in Cloudflare R2 and served through media.orboro.net. Articles
      may also display images hosted elsewhere; loading them contacts their hosts. Images
      published on the site are publicly accessible. When content is published, the server
      notifies IndexNow of its public URL and a WebSub hub of the public RSS feed URL.
      These publication notifications do not forward visitor request information.
    </p>

    <h2>Service providers and storage</h2>
    <p>
      Cloudflare hosts the site, its D1 database and R2 images, sends member account email
      and runs the Turnstile check. Its
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Privacy Policy
      </a>
      describes its handling of information. Google processes analytics information under
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Google's Privacy Policy
      </a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Choices and contact</h2>
    <p>
      Use <strong>Cookie preferences</strong> in the footer to change your analytics choice.
      Withdrawing consent removes this site's Google Analytics cookies and reloads the page
      to stop the running tag. If local storage is unavailable, your choice lasts only for the
      current page session, including in-site navigation, and is lost on a full reload.
      When local storage is available, changing the choice also updates other open tabs.
      This choice controls analytics; necessary member and administrator session cookies, the
      Turnstile check on account forms, and external images described above are not controlled
      by the banner.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can also block analytics scripts using the tools linked above and manage
      cookies through your browser. Blocking analytics does not stop Cloudflare from processing the requests
      needed to serve the site. For questions or requests about your information, contact JD
      through the platform profiles linked on the homepage. What can be located or deleted
      depends on the information held and the relevant provider's controls.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      This policy may be updated occasionally. The "last updated" date at the top of the page
      will reflect any changes.
    </p>

    <hr />
  </section>
  <Sidebar slot="sidebar" categories={categories} recentPosts={recentPosts} />
  </SidebarLayout>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Same columns as a blog post. */

  section {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  h3 {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }
</style>
